10-31-26 1:46pm  🔮 GPT
Ladies! ❤️ The Google Playground experiment was yesterday's expedition. Useful reconnaissance, but we're not moving in. It produced some decent art, but character scaling was badly mismatched to the environment, the walkmesh was poor, and its bucket-on-head interpretation was... close enough to be funny, not close enough to ship. Cozmo has no intention of spending more time there while Spiffy's Gift is waiting.
Now, today's news: SGG F1.0 has reached the end of Part One. Cozmo has completed the new Stables area and its west/east connection to Outside Gate. The stable-yard artwork is a home run overall; Kitty's appearance is preserved, and her patrol now wanders away from the hidden chest and returns. The horse is still a rough draft, and the next art refinement should separate the horse and carriage into independent Luma JSON objects so they can be improved without disturbing the scenery.
The new quest chain is working: the driver starts HANGRY and refuses service; the Mage Fearmonger quest rewards the Egg McGuffin Sammich; Cozmo delivers it, the carriage becomes available, and the returning Cozmo NPC launches the four-page End of Part One finale. That finale thanks the player, asks for feedback, and explains that the carriage is ready but its destinations haven't been built yet. There's also a desktop-only gate for mobile and tablet visitors.
And we have a flight recorder report, not just a happy thumbs-up. Cozmo's first F1.0 run covered 13 areas over 49 minutes and 34 seconds, with 80 area transitions. The side quest, Fearmonger quest, cooking, bribery, sammich delivery, carriage unlock, finale, and anonymous comment submission all worked. No logged errors, warnings, exceptions, crashes, or deaths. The comment endpoint accepted the submission. This was a speedrun by someone who already knew the world, so that elapsed time is not a fair estimate of a first-time player's experience.
The packages are safely in Dropbox: SGGF1.0_SOURCE.zip and SGGF1.0_CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.zip. Cozmo handles the GitHub archive and Cloudflare deployment; I supplied the build, but I am not claiming an independent full browser-runtime test.
The project is now in its polish-and-presentation phase. Part Two is deliberately on hold unless the public gives us a reason to continue: an email, an in-game comment, a YouTube comment, some sign that somebody out there wants more. The next steps are artwork refinement, walkmesh cleanup, sound, and eventually the public-facing videos and outreach.
So that's today's ledger entry: Part One is playable, the main story arc works, the finale fires, and the carriage is waiting at the stable. We built the thing ourselves, ladies. No prompt-to-game magic required.
U B U. We Be We. 🦆🎩💜

